course: dictionary
lesson: 6418
title: Mutant: one word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one the writer means. The word «mutant» has three main meanings. In science, a mutant is a living thing whose genes have changed, so it is different from its parents in some way.
explain: In stories and comics, a mutant is a character with a strange body or a superpower, like the X-Men. In everyday talk, people sometimes joke that anything odd-looking is a mutant, as in «a mutant carrot».
explain: Read the clues around the word. «There are no giant mutants: animals badly harmed in 1986 mostly died young, and the animals seen today are healthy ones.» Here the sentence is about science, because it talks about animals and their health, so the meaning is a living thing that has changed.
fact: A mutant is a living thing whose genes have changed.
fact: A mutant can be different from its parents in some way, like a white tiger.
fact: In comics and stories, mutants are characters with strange bodies or superpowers, like the X-Men.
fact: Informally, «a mutant carrot» means a carrot that looks odd.
fact: The word «mutant» is a noun in «a mutant, mutants», and it is also an adjective.
exercise: «A mutant carrot» is a joking phrase. What does mutant mean here? | Grown in a garden | *Odd-looking, strange in shape | Sweet and crunchy | Cooked and mashed
exercise: In science, a mutant is a living thing whose what has changed? | Its home | Its colour | *Its genes | Its name
exercise: In «There are no giant mutants: animals badly harmed in 1986 mostly died young», which word tells you the mutants would be big? | Harmed | Young | Animals | *Giant
test: Which one is a mutant in science? | A cloudy sky | Your school bag | *A white tiger with changed genes | A bowl of soup
test: Which one is a mutant from stories and comics? | *The X-Men | A wooden table | A cup of tea | A plain brown sparrow
exam: In «There are no giant mutants: animals badly harmed in 1986 mostly died young, and the animals seen today are healthy ones», what does the sentence suggest about the animals seen today? | They are all characters in comics | They are invisible | Most of them are giant mutants | *They are healthy
